cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use shockVoF in your work, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "shockVoF: A density-based Volume-of-Fluid solver for compressible two-phase flows with surface tension in OpenFOAM"
abstract: >-
  shockVoF is a density-based Volume-of-Fluid solver module for compressible
  two-phase flows in OpenFOAM 14. It is based on the six-equation model with
  ideal-gas and stiffened-gas phases, instantaneous pressure relaxation and an
  additional mixture total-energy equation, integrated with MUSCL/rho-THINC
  reconstruction, an HLLC Riemann solver, SSP Runge-Kutta time stepping and a
  flux-corrected-transport limiter. Its field of application is high-speed
  atomization of liquids.
authors:
